(361, 'MARKDOWN', U&'# Engineering summary (GREENFIELD)\000a\000a## Outcome\000aGREENFIELD workflow finished; release readiness is READY_WITH_CONDITIONS.\000a\000a## Plan\000a10 engineering tasks, critical path 17h.\000a\000a## Quality\000a7 planned test cases, acceptance coverage 100%.\000a\000a## Risk\000a2 risks recorded; review verdict APPROVE_WITH_COMMENTS.\000a\000a## Governance\000aApprovals granted: final-approval. Generated code was never executed.\000a\000a', TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE '2026-11-08 07:48:29.357963+00', 'engineering-summary.md', '1cf511331e8bd5eba511c1907f3a2690856d16ca59d14c1d5e88890c13d5f1d8', 'ACCEPTED', NULL, '7cabcc01-3391-4536-a0ac-dcb66e8a4f56/v1/engineering-summary.md', 'engineering-summary', 1, '7cabcc01-3391-4536-a0ac-dcb66e8a4f56'),
(362, 'MARKDOWN', U&'# Requirement analysis\000a\000a**Scenario:** GREENFIELD\000a\000aBuild a URL shortener with custom aliases, expiration, redirects and click analytics.\000a\000a## Functional requirements\000a- FR-1: Create short URLs from valid http/https URLs\000a- FR-2: Redirect a short code to the original URL\000a- FR-3: Support unique custom aliases\000a- FR-4: Support expiration dates\000a- FR-5: Track clicks with timestamps and referrer, and expose analytics\000a\000a## Acceptance criteria\000a- AC-1 [AGREED]: Given a valid URL, POST /api/v1/urls returns 201 and a unique collision-resistant code\000a- AC-2 [AGREED]: Given an active, unexpired code, GET returns 302 with the original URL\000a- AC-3 [AGREED]: Given a free alias it is used; a duplicate alias returns 409\000a- AC-4 [AGREED]: Given an expired link, redirect returns 410 and past dates are rejected on creation\000a- AC-5 [AGREED]: Each redirect increments the click count; analytics returns totals, referrers and daily clicks\000a- AC-6 [AGREED]: javascript:, data: and file: URLs are rejected with 400\000a\000a## Ambiguities and clarification questions\000a- AMB-1 (MINOR): Allowed alias length and characters?  \000a  Provisional assumption: 3-32 chars of [A-Za-z0-9_-]\000a- AMB-2 (MINOR): Which timezone applies to expiration dates?  \000a  Provisional assumption: UTC\000a- AMB-3 (MINOR): 301 or 302?  \000a  Provisional assumption: 302 so every click is counted\000a\000a> SIMULATED RESPONSE: produced by deterministic rules in MockLLMProvider, not by a real LLM.\000a', TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE '2026-11-08 07:48:29.493785+00', 'requirements-analysis.md', 'fd4c8a9ea8b503a754fff451c013cf182674a384ab55ecd3b0a1ba2cb1c6f9e2', 'STAGED', NULL, '65168ee0-2264-4d95-87ae-070d536c5fc5/v1/requirements-analysis.md', 'requirements', 1, '65168ee0-2264-4d95-87ae-070d536c5fc5'),
(363, 'MARKDOWN', U&'# Task plan\000a\000a| Task | Title | Hours | Depends on |\000a|---|---|---|---|\000a| T1 | Project skeleton and configuration | 2 | [] |\000a| T2 | Data model and constraints | 3 | [T1] |\000a| T3 | Short code generator | 2 | [T1] |\000a| T4 | Create-URL API with validation | 4 | [T2, T3] |\000a| T5 | Redirect endpoint | 3 | [T2] |\000a| T6 | Custom alias handling | 2 | [T4] |\000a| T7 | Expiration handling | 2 | [T4, T5] |\000a| T8 | Click tracking and analytics API | 5 | [T5] |\000a| T9 | Error handling and OpenAPI | 2 | [T4, T5] |\000a| T10 | Automated tests | 6 | [T9] |\000a\000aParallel groups: [[T1], [T2, T3], [T5, T4], [T8, T6, T7, T9], [T10]]\000a\000aCritical path: [T1, T2, T4, T9, T10] (17h)\000a', TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE '2026-11-08 07:48:29.521818+00', 'task-plan.md', '6c2e81f65d07ea7f0deb2d2c8bae41230e4ab05f6148982a53522925298128c0', 'STAGED', NULL, '65168ee0-2264-4d95-87ae-070d536c5fc5/v1/task-plan.md', 'planning', 1, '65168ee0-2264-4d95-87ae-070d536c5fc5');   
