(519, 'MARKDOWN', U&'# Requirement analysis\000a\000a**Scenario:** GREENFIELD\000a\000aBuild a URL shortener with custom aliases, expiration, redirects and click analytics.\000a\000a## Functional requirements\000a- FR-1: Create short URLs from valid http/https URLs\000a- FR-2: Redirect a short code to the original URL\000a- FR-3: Support unique custom aliases\000a- FR-4: Support expiration dates\000a- FR-5: Track clicks with timestamps and referrer, and expose analytics\000a\000a## Acceptance criteria\000a- AC-1 [AGREED]: Given a valid URL, POST /api/v1/urls returns 201 and a unique collision-resistant code\000a- AC-2 [AGREED]: Given an active, unexpired code, GET returns 302 with the original URL\000a- AC-3 [AGREED]: Given a free alias it is used; a duplicate alias returns 409\000a- AC-4 [AGREED]: Given an expired link, redirect returns 410 and past dates are rejected on creation\000a- AC-5 [AGREED]: Each redirect increments the click count; analytics returns totals, referrers and daily clicks\000a- AC-6 [AGREED]: javascript:, data: and file: URLs are rejected with 400\000a\000a## Ambiguities and clarification questions\000a- AMB-1 (MINOR): Allowed alias length and characters?  \000a  Provisional assumption: 3-32 chars of [A-Za-z0-9_-]\000a- AMB-2 (MINOR): Which timezone applies to expiration dates?  \000a  Provisional assumption: UTC\000a- AMB-3 (MINOR): 301 or 302?  \000a  Provisional assumption: 302 so every click is counted\000a\000a> SIMULATED RESPONSE: produced by deterministic rules in MockLLMProvider, not by a real LLM.\000a', TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE '2026-11-08 07:49:30.666642+00', 'requirements-analysis.md', 'fd4c8a9ea8b503a754fff451c013cf182674a384ab55ecd3b0a1ba2cb1c6f9e2', 'ACCEPTED', NULL, '282cba34-21db-4cbc-8bc6-36d1097061e7/v1/requirements-analysis.md', 'requirements', 1, '282cba34-21db-4cbc-8bc6-36d1097061e7');            
