(536, 'MARKDOWN', U&'# Enhance the existing URL shortener so expired links are deactivated automatically.\000a\000aScenario: BROWNFIELD\000a\000a## Requirements\000a- FR-1: Redirects to expired links keep returning HTTP 410 (existing behaviour preserved)\000a- FR-2: A scheduled job automatically deactivates links whose expiration date has passed\000a- FR-3: Existing API contracts remain backward compatible\000a\000a## Planned files\000a- CREATE src/main/java/com/example/shortener/scheduler/ExpiredUrlDeactivationScheduler.java\000a- MODIFY src/main/java/com/example/shortener/repository/ShortUrlRepository.java\000a- MODIFY src/main/java/com/example/shortener/service/UrlShortenerService.java\000a- MODIFY src/main/java/com/example/shortener/entity/ShortUrl.java\000a', TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE '2026-11-08 07:49:32.332832+00', 'change-documentation.md', '5002fbca2ac1b0de060c5e0f77dc58ccc73ef907dc1f01791a9412d318c41235', 'ACCEPTED', NULL, 'a47d06be-3fc3-47d4-ae05-4d1cb49dc235/v1/change-documentation.md', 'documentation', 1, 'a47d06be-3fc3-47d4-ae05-4d1cb49dc235'),
