(759, 'MARKDOWN', U&'# Requirement analysis\000a\000a**Scenario:** BROWNFIELD\000a\000aEnhance the existing URL shortener so expired links are deactivated automatically.\000a\000a## Functional requirements\000a- FR-1: Redirects to expired links keep returning HTTP 410 (existing behaviour preserved)\000a- FR-2: A scheduled job automatically deactivates links whose expiration date has passed\000a- FR-3: Existing API contracts remain backward compatible\000a\000a## Acceptance criteria\000a- AC-1 [AGREED]: Given links past their expiration, when the job runs, then active=false for all of them\000a- AC-2 [AGREED]: Given an expired link, redirect returns 410 before and after the job runs\000a- AC-3 [AGREED]: Existing request and response contracts of all /api/v1/urls endpoints are unchanged\000a- AC-4 [AGREED]: Running the job twice changes nothing the second time and never exceeds the batch size\000a\000a## Ambiguities and clarification questions\000a- AMB-1 (MINOR): How soon after expiry must a link be deactivated?  \000a  Provisional assumption: Within 5 minutes via a scheduled job\000a- AMB-2 (MINOR): Is there a grace period after expiry?  \000a  Provisional assumption: No grace period\000a\000a> SIMULATED RESPONSE: produced by deterministic rules in MockLLMProvider, not by a real LLM.\000a', TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE '2026-11-08 08:03:40.802631+00', 'requirements-analysis.md', 'b7f41c35fc394acf740848904536853e381c94f98bab5760e3dd3da636ec9114', 'ACCEPTED', NULL, 'dda332fa-b8cf-4968-9f96-08f41b38a510/v1/requirements-analysis.md', 'requirements', 1, 'dda332fa-b8cf-4968-9f96-08f41b38a510');       
