(908, 'MARKDOWN', U&'# Requirement analysis\000a\000a**Scenario:** AMBIGUOUS\000a\000aRequest to improve performance and reliability of the existing URL shortener; no measurable targets given.\000a\000a## Functional requirements\000a- FR-1: Improve the speed of the URL shortener (operations and metrics unspecified)\000a- FR-2: Make the URL shortener more reliable (meaning of reliability unspecified)\000a\000a## Acceptance criteria\000a- AC-1 [PROVISIONAL]: Redirect p95 latency <= 50 ms at 500 requests/s on one instance (provisional)\000a- AC-2 [PROVISIONAL]: Redirect availability >= 99.9% over a month; measured by health probes (provisional)\000a- AC-3 [PROVISIONAL]: No committed short URL is lost across an application restart (provisional)\000a- AC-4 [PROVISIONAL]: A failure while recording a click never breaks the redirect (provisional)\000a\000a## Ambiguities and clarification questions\000a- AMB-1 (BLOCKING): Which operations (redirect, creation, analytics) are in scope, and what p95/p99 latency and throughput are required?  \000a  Provisional assumption: Redirect p95 <= 50 ms at 500 requests/s on a single instance\000a- AMB-2 (BLOCKING): Does reliable mean an availability SLO, durability of data, or graceful degradation (or all three)?  \000a  Provisional assumption: 99.9% monthly availability for redirects and no loss of committed URL records\000a- AMB-3 (BLOCKING): May new infrastructure such as a shared cache be introduced, or must we stay on the current database only?  \000a  Provisional assumption: A shared cache for redirect lookups may be introduced\000a- AMB-4 (MINOR): Do baseline measurements exist?  \000a  Provisional assumption: A baseline load test is run before any change\000a\000a> SIMULATED RESPONSE: produced by deterministic rules in MockLLMProvider, not by a real LLM.\000a', TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE '2026-11-08 08:05:26.135529+00', 'requirements-analysis.md', '57af3d227935330687fe986a91ed74cf9e82909459a9b010a3545d346cb168c7', 'ACCEPTED', NULL, 'ae3097b0-7968-499e-a890-d57a9ead63b0/v1/requirements-analysis.md', 'requirements', 1, 'ae3097b0-7968-499e-a890-d57a9ead63b0'),
(909, 'MARKDOWN', U&'# Task plan\000a\000a| Task | Title | Hours | Depends on |\000a|---|---|---|---|\000a| P1 | Establish baseline with a load test | 4 | [] |\000a| P2 | Profile the redirect path | 3 | [] |\000a| P3 | Add a redirect lookup cache | 8 | [P2] |\000a| P4 | Record clicks asynchronously | 6 | [P2] |\000a| P5 | Review database indexes and queries | 3 | [P1] |\000a| P6 | Add timeouts and graceful degradation | 6 | [P1] |\000a| P7 | Add liveness and readiness probes | 3 | [P6] |\000a| P8 | Run load and fault tests against the agreed targets | 8 | [P3, P4, P5, P7] |\000a\000aParallel groups: [[P1, P2], [P5, P6, P3, P4], [P7], [P8]]\000a\000aCritical path: [P1, P6, P7, P8] (21h)\000a', TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE '2026-11-08 08:05:26.216863+00', 'task-plan.md', '31c4f76ff9c3206c952b56ac93cd278514edf774d704f8af3bb5d57314d343a8', 'ACCEPTED', NULL, 'ae3097b0-7968-499e-a890-d57a9ead63b0/v1/task-plan.md', 'planning', 1, 'ae3097b0-7968-499e-a890-d57a9ead63b0'),
(910, 'MARKDOWN', U&'# Architecture\000a\000aLayered Spring Boot application with relational persistence\000a\000a## Components\000a- **UrlShortenerController**: Thin REST layer\000a- **UrlShortenerService**: Business rules and transactions\000a- **ShortUrlRepository / UrlClickRepository**: Spring Data JPA persistence\000a- **RedirectCache**: Shared cache in front of redirect lookups\000a- **AsyncClickRecorder**: Buffered click writes off the redirect path\000a\000a## Decisions\000a- AD-1 Layered Spring Boot monolith - Smallest operational footprint that meets the requirement (alternatives: Microservices)\000a- AD-2 Introduce a shared cache for redirects - Redirects are read-heavy; caching removes the DB read from the hot path (alternatives: In-process cache; read replicas)\000a', TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE '2026-11-08 08:05:26.239875+00', 'architecture.md', '273e7e99f120ab071b6cb481e4e5467fa3d8bf42983a513901526d1dc35eb5b6', 'ACCEPTED', NULL, 'ae3097b0-7968-499e-a890-d57a9ead63b0/v1/architecture.md', 'architecture', 1, 'ae3097b0-7968-499e-a890-d57a9ead63b0'); 
